   "source": [
    "# Practical 4: Gradient Descent Algorithm\n",
    "**Objective:** Implement Gradient Descent to find the local minima of a function.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example:** Find the local minima of y = (x + 3)² starting from x = 2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Define Function and its Derivative"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def f(x):\n",
    "    return (x + 3) ** 2\n",
    "\n",
    "def df(x):\n",
    "    return 2 * (x + 3)  # Derivative: dy/dx"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Gradient Descent"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Local Minima: x = -2.999929, y = 0.000000\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "def gradient_descent(start, learning_rate=0.1, epochs=50):\n",
    "    x = start\n",
    "    history = [(x, f(x))]\n",
    "\n",
    "    for _ in range(epochs):\n",
    "        x = x - learning_rate * df(x)\n",
    "        history.append((x, f(x)))\n",
    "\n",
    "    return x, f(x), history\n",
    "\n",
    "x_min, y_min, history = gradient_descent(start=2, learning_rate=0.1, epochs=50)\n",
    "print(f\"Local Minima: x = {x_min:.6f}, y = {y_min:.6f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
